<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Taunt Skill</h1>
<p>Class and level:
</p>
<pre> Barbarian Level 30
 Dark Knight Level 30
</pre>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre> taunt &lt;target&gt;
 taunt              (in a fight: your opponent)
</pre>
<p>Confident - or perhaps overconfident - in their own combat prowess, the 
Barbarian may (if successful) taunt their enemies. 
If successfully executed during battle, the opponent loses focus for a 
while and is slow to return attacks; taunting them again before they 
recover has no effect. If successfully executed outside of combat, the 
victim will initiate an attack in response to the ruthless taunting, 
unless they are sitting, resting or stunned.
</p><p>Each taunt takes 40 endurance. A badly failed taunt makes your target 
attack you, and a failed taunt ends a defence (see <a cmd='#'>Help defend</a>). You 
can't taunt someone much larger than yourself, and you can taunt another 
player only when both of you have signed the book of blood.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre> &gt; <a cmd='#'>Help defend</a>
